# SimpleX Chat — system floor.
#
# SimpleX is here because it is the only usable messenger with no user
# identifier at all: no phone number, no username, no account for a server to
# hand over. That is a strictly better metadata story than Signal's phone
# numbers and a categorically better one than Matrix's federated room state.
#
# NETWORK=allow rather than tor, for the same reason the Tor Browser scope is
# allow: SimpleX has its own SOCKS setting, and forcing it into the system onion
# netns on top of that is Tor-over-Tor. Turn on SimpleX's own Tor option, or
# set NETWORK=tor here and leave SimpleX's own setting off — not both.
NETWORK=allow
FILES=portal
CAMERA=deny
MIC=deny
USB=deny
SENSORS=deny
